I don't think establishing this as a standard in writing is such a good
idea, but yes, I agree that that's standard in practice. The concrete
evidence that supports this subjective idea is that {broda ko'a} and {ko'a
broda} in the absence of any other sumti are different. So the x1 being
before the selbri is "special" while anything else being before the selbri
is not.

mu'o mi'e latros

